27	1300	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Standard penetration testing is insufficient for AI. Large Language Models (LLMs) are susceptible to unique attacks like prompt injection, where malicious inputs trick the model into bypassing safety filters or leaking training data.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Neozaar’s Adversarial Defense service combines proactive "Red Teaming" (simulated attacks) with runtime "Guardrails" to filter malicious prompts and unsafe outputs in real-time, ensuring your AI agents behave as intended.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Our service covers the full spectrum of offensive testing and defensive implementation for AI systems:&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>1. Offensive Testing (Red Teaming)&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Simulated Attacks: Automated and manual AI Red Teaming to identify weaknesses.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Compliance Testing: Comprehensive LLM application testing aligned with the OWASP Top 10 for LLMs.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Robustness Checks: Stress testing the model against adversarial inputs and manipulation attempts.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>2. Runtime Protection &amp; Guardrails&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Input/Output Filtering: Deployment of real-time guardrails to sanitize model inputs and outputs.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Threat Mitigation: Active mitigation of prompt injection attacks and jailbreak attempts.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Anomaly Detection: Detection of hallucinations and toxic or biased model outputs.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>3. Pipeline Security&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>RAG Security: Vulnerability assessment of Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Data Integrity: Analysis of training data for potential poisoning or corruption risks.&nbsp;</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"><br></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Neozaar utilizes a "Think Like an Attacker" methodology to secure your AI infrastructure:&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 1: Discovery &amp; Analysis: We begin by reviewing system prompts, RAG architecture, and application endpoints to understand the logic and potential attack surface.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 2: Adversarial Attack Simulation: We deploy a library of proprietary adversarial attack patterns, targeting the model to bypass safety filters and extract sensitive data.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 3: Expert Validation: Our human-in-the-loop experts analyze successful breaches to distinguish between model hallucinations and genuine security flaws.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	["Secured AI Logic: AI agents that resist manipulation and adhere to defined behavioral boundaries. ","Data Integrity: Prevention of training data leakage and intellectual property theft. ","Brand Protection: Elimination of toxic or biased outputs that could damage reputation. ","Verified Safety: Confidence that pre-deployment safety validation has been rigorously tested. "]	<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Intentional Manipulation: Protection against malicious Prompt Injection attacks.&nbsp;</span></li><li>System Exposure: Preventing accidental disclosure of sensitive system prompts.&nbsp;</li><li>Unsafe Outputs: Mitigating toxic, biased, or harmful model responses.&nbsp;</li><li>IP Theft: Blocking attempts to steal intellectual property via model inversion techniques.&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0px"><br></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>			[]	2026-02-24 17:42:01.004	2026-07-24 12:33:39.067
130	1524		<ul><li><span>SaaS\napplication data protection assessment</span></li><li><span>Cloud-native workload backup configuration</span></li><li><span>Backup policy design for SaaS platforms</span></li><li><span>Centralized backup monitoring setup</span></li><li><span>Recovery testing and validation</span></li><li><span>Data retention and compliance policy alignment</span></li></ul><p style=" margin: 0"></p>		[]	<p class="MsoNormal"></p><ul><li>Data loss from accidental deletion in SaaS platforms</li><li>Limited native backup capabilities in many SaaS tools</li><li>Ransomware targeting cloud-stored business data</li><li>Lack of centralized visibility across SaaS environments</li><li>Compliance risks due to improper data retention</li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0"></p>	<p class="MsoNormal"></p><ul><li>Unified protection for both SaaS applications and\ncloud-native workloads</li><li>Granular recovery capabilities to restore individual data objects</li><li>Centralized visibility across distributed cloud applications</li><li>Designed for modern cloud-first enterprise environments</li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0"></p>	<p class="MsoNormal">Neozaar ensures that cloud convenience does not come at the\ncost of data protection. By securing both SaaS and cloud-native environments\nwith automated backups and fast recovery capabilities, organizations gain\ncomplete control over their critical business data regardless of where it\nresides.</p><p style=" margin: 0"></p>	["AvePoint","Veeam","Microsoft","Google","Druva"]	2026-06-09 11:11:09.702	2026-06-29 05:19:03.265
21	1294		<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Multi-cloud and hybrid identity directory integration.&nbsp;</span></li><li>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) design and implementation.&nbsp;</li><li>Automated provisioning/de-provisioning workflow setup.&nbsp;</li><li>Policy-based access enforcement (context, geography, time).&nbsp;</li><li>Periodic access certification campaigns.&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>		[]	<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Security gaps from delayed manual de-provisioning of former employees.&nbsp;</span></li><li>High IT costs associated with manual user management and password resets.&nbsp;</li><li>"Password fatigue" leading to weak, reused credentials.&nbsp;</li><li>Fragmented visibility across disparate SaaS and cloud identity silos.&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><div><br></div><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Vendor-Agnostic Federation: Integrates seamlessly with Azure Entra ID, Okta, or Google Workspace.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px">Context-Aware Adaptive Policies: Changes authentication requirements in real-time based on risk signals.&nbsp;</p><p style="margin: 0px">Zero-Trust Foundation: Built on the principle of "verify explicitly" for every connection.&nbsp;</p><p style=" margin: 0px"><br></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Neozaar transforms identity from a security bottleneck into a business enabler. We provide the "plumbing" that allows your users to access what they need instantly, while giving security teams the "brakes" to stop unauthorized access immediately.&nbsp;</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"><br></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	["IBM","CyberArk","Wiz","Azure","AWS","Google"]	2026-02-24 09:27:33.518	2026-07-24 12:35:57.841
80	1353	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Traditional annual penetration tests often miss vulnerabilities that emerge between audits. Neozaar’s CTEM service provides ongoing visibility into your evolving attack surface by combining automated scanning with expert vulnerability assessment.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>We act as a proactive risk management partner, identifying and categorizing risks by severity and business impact. This ensures your teams focus remediation efforts on the most urgent threats first, shifting your security stance from reactive to predictive.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Our service covers the comprehensive identification and management of vulnerabilities across your digital footprint:&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Vulnerability Scanning: Continuous scanning of network, application, and infrastructure layers.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Cloud Review: In-depth review of cloud misconfigurations and access policies.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Risk Classification: Mapping of vulnerabilities to severity levels and business impact.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Remediation Roadmap: Creation of a clear roadmap with tracking for remediation progress.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Human Defense: Employee security awareness training and phishing simulations.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Neozaar utilizes a continuous, closed-loop methodology to manage exposure:&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 1: Mapping: We perform External Attack Surface Mapping to identify all internet-facing assets and "shadow IT".&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 2: Simulation: We validate existing controls through Penetration Testing Simulation, mimicking real-world attacker behaviors.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 3: Monitoring: We deploy automated security audits and configuration drift detection to alert on unauthorized changes.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 4: Risk-Based Prioritization: We prioritize patches based on real-world exploitability and specific business risk, not just CVSS scores.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	["Strategic Advantage: Transformation of vulnerability management from a \\"chore\\" into a strategic advantage.","Verified Security: Closed-Loop Remediation ensures that applied patches have actually fixed the issue. ","Business Context: Understanding of exactly which bugs hurt business revenue via Business Context Scoring. ","Visualized Risk: Attack Path Analysis visualizing how small vulnerabilities can lead to critical compromises. ","Financial Benefits: Readiness for M&A due diligence and potential reduction in cyber insurance premiums. "]	<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Compliance Gaps: Addressing gaps with regulations like GDPR, HIPAA, and PCI-DSS.&nbsp;</span></li><li>Attack Surface Growth: Managing the unmanaged growth of cloud and SaaS tool attack surfaces.&nbsp;</li><li>Data Exposure: Fixing misconfigurations that lead to accidental data exposure.&nbsp;</li><li>Risk Quantification: Overcoming the inability to quantify cyber risk for executive stakeholders.</li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>			[]	2026-02-26 09:02:05.707	2026-07-24 12:39:10.882
