79	1352	<div style="text-align: justify"><span>Containers introduce new security risks, including vulnerable base images and insecure orchestration settings. A "Shift-Left" approach involves verifying the integrity of the image before it ever hits the registry.&nbsp;</span></div><div style="text-align: justify"><br></div><div style="text-align: justify">Neozaar provides a complete hardening service that covers the entire lifecycle—from image signing and vulnerability scanning to the implementation of Kubernetes Admission Controllers. We ensure that only "trusted" and "scanned" containers are allowed to run in your production cluster, wrapping your microservices in a layer of "Zero Trust."</div><div><br></div>	<p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0px"><span>Our service covers end-to-end security for containerized workloads:</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0px"><span>Image Security: Dockerfile and Image review, including Distroless/Minimal image conversion.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0px"><span>Cluster Audit: Comprehensive Kubernetes cluster configuration audit.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0px"><span>Access Control: Kubernetes RBAC (Role-Based Access Control) hardening.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0px"><span>Secret Management: Implementation of secure secret management (HashiCorp Vault/Cloud Secrets).</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0px"><span>Admission Control: Implementation of Admission Controllers (e.g., Kyverno, OPA Gatekeeper).</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0px"><span>Network Security: Network policy implementation for micro-segmentation.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Neozaar utilizes a "Full-Stack" methodology to secure containers from the code level to the runtime environment:</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Step 1: Shift-Left Verification: We integrate security into the Registry (Harbor/ECR/ACR), scanning and signing images to verify integrity before deployment.</span></li><li><span>Step 2: Orchestration Hardening: We audit and harden the Kubernetes control plane, enforcing "Least Privilege" for microservices and restricting broad permissions.</span></li><li><span>Step 3: Runtime Defense: We implement runtime security observability and active admission controllers to block non-compliant workloads and monitor for anomalies.</span></li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	["Reduced Attack Surface: Minimized risk through Distroless images and rigorous vulnerability scanning.","Regulatory Compliance: Environment hardened to meet PCI and HIPAA requirements for containers.","Zero Trust Posture: Trusted execution environment where even a compromised container cannot compromise the cluster","Operational Visibility: Deep visibility into inter-container traffic and runtime behavior.","Secure Supply Chain: A private secure container registry that ensures only verified code runs in production."]	<div><ul><li><span>Vulnerable Images: Risks arising from the use of vulnerable third-party container images.</span></li><li><span>Privilege Escalation: "Privileged" containers causing host breakouts.</span></li><li><span>Visibility Gaps: Lack of visibility into east-west inter-container traffic.</span></li><li><span>Permission Sprawl: Overly broad cluster permissions that increase the blast radius of a breach.</span></li></ul></div>			[]	2026-02-26 08:02:26.963	2026-07-24 12:43:13.357
