78	1351	<div><span>Cloud misconfigurations are the leading cause of data breaches. When infrastructure is defined as code, security must also be defined as code.</span></div><div><span>This service focuses on scanning IaC templates for misconfigured S3 buckets, overly permissive IAM roles, and insecure network groups. By catching these "infrastructure flaws" in the IDE or Git repository, Neozaar ensures that insecure environments are never even created, significantly reducing the cloud attack surface.</span></div><div><span>Scope</span></div><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<div><span>Our service covers the security of your infrastructure code from development to deployment:</span></div><div><ul><li><span>Template Review: Comprehensive review of Terraform, Bicep, Helm charts, and CloudFormation templates.</span></li><li><span>Policy Implementation: Implementation of Policy-as-Code (using OPA/Rego) to automate governance.</span></li><li><span>Developer Integration: Seamless integration with IDEs (VS Code/IntelliJ) for real-time feedback.</span></li><li><span>Audit: Security audit of existing cloud configurations to identify legacy risks.</span></li><li><span>Drift Management: Detection of drift between defined code and actual cloud state (identifying manual console changes).</span></li></ul></div>	<div><span>Neozaar utilizes a "Secure-by-Design" methodology to embed security into the infrastructure lifecycle:</span></div><div><ul><li><span>Step 1: Shift-Left Scanning: We implement pre-provisioning security checks directly in the CI/CD pipeline and developer workstations.</span></li><li><span>Step 2: Standardization: We provide standardized "Secure Architecture" templates to ensure all new infrastructure starts secure.</span></li><li><span>Step 3: Automated Enforcement: We deploy Policy-as-Code to automatically block non-compliant deployments and suggest remediation.</span></li></ul></div>	["Reduced Risk: Reduction of cloud attack surface by up to 80% before resources are even provisioned.","Proactive Security: Transition from reactive security (fixing console errors) to proactive security (coding it right the first time).","Compliance Assurance: Automated Compliance-as-Code checks against SOC2, HIPAA, and CIS Benchmarks.","Operational Consistency: Multi-cloud consistency with the same security rules applied across AWS and Azure."]	<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Insecure Defaults: Prevention of deployments using insecure "Default" cloud settings.</span></li><li><span>Compliance Violations: Stopping compliance violations before they reach production environments.</span></li><li><span>Shadow Infrastructure: Elimination of "Shadow Infrastructure" created by developers outside of governance.</span></li><li><span>Permission Complexity: Simplification of managing complex multi-cloud permissions and identities.</span></li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>			[]	2026-02-26 07:45:04.618	2026-07-24 12:45:42.998
