83	1356	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Most AI systems today are built on top of open-source models (Hugging Face), third-party libraries, and external APIs. This creates a massive "Supply Chain" risk where a single compromised dependency or "poisoned" base model can compromise your entire application.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>This service implements a rigorous verification process for your AI stack. We audit your AI Bill of Materials (AI-BOM), verify model signatures, and monitor for "Model Drift" or tampering in production. This ensures that the AI you deployed yesterday hasn't been subtly altered by an attacker today.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Our service covers the end-to-end integrity of your AI model lifecycle:&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Audit: Comprehensive audit of third-party model dependencies and libraries.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Registry Setup: Setup of secure model registries to centralize and control AI assets.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Versioning: Implementation of "Model Versioning" with strict security checkpoints.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Adversarial Monitoring: Continuous monitoring for adversarial model degradation or unauthorized changes.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Provenance: Verification of data provenance to ensure training data origin is legitimate.</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	<p style="margin: 0px"><span>Neozaar utilizes a "Chain of Custody" methodology to secure your AI supply chain:&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 1: AI-BOM Generation: We generate and audit a comprehensive AI Bill of Materials (AI-BOM) to map every component and dependency in your stack.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 2: Hardening &amp; Signing: We implement cryptographic signing of model weights and perform base model vulnerability scanning to establish a "known good" state.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span><br></span></p><p style="margin: 0px"><span>Step 3: Continuous Integrity: We deploy continuous monitors to detect "Hidden Backdoors" or drift in production, ensuring the model remains untampered with over time.&nbsp;</span></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>	["Trusted Foundation: A verified \\"Chain of Custody\\" for your AI, ensuring systems are authentic and untampered.","Risk Reduction: Mitigation of risks from \\"poisoned\\" open-source models and compromised libraries. ","Regulatory Alignment: Alignment with NIST AI 100-1 and SLSA frameworks for compliance. ","Operational Integrity: Assurance that high-integrity automated decision-making systems remain unbiased and secure. "]	<p style="margin: 0px"></p><ul><li><span>Model Poisoning: Detection of "Poisoned" open-source models before they enter production.&nbsp;</span></li><li>Supply Chain Attacks: Prevention of attacks via compromised ML libraries (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow vulnerabilities).&nbsp;</li><li>Unauthorized Changes: Alerting on unauthorized changes to production model weights.&nbsp;</li><li>Data Bias: Identifying the use of biased or unethically sourced training data.&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><p style=" margin: 0px"></p>			[]	2026-02-26 09:25:20.665	2026-07-24 12:41:47.683
